<title>UK: Shell shares firm, NatWest positive.</title>
<headline>Shell shares firm, NatWest positive.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Shell Transport and Trading Co Plc firmed on Tuesday, boosted by a strong overnight performance in the U.S. and a positive research note from NatWest, dealers said.</p>
<p>Market sources said NatWest had reaffirmed its positive stance on Shell and British Petroleum Co Plc and increased its dividend forecasts for the two stocks.</p>
<p>&quot;NatWest have been pushing Shell, and it was firm in the U.S. overnight,&quot; one market-maker said.</p>
<p>Shell shares were up 13p at 429-1/2 by 0923 GMT, with BP up 12p at 849-1/2.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
